The iconic Dock Gregory is one of the people I truly admire. I have several of these vintage #ebonymagazine & I use them for mix media collages. This particular magazine is in near perfect condition and I don’t want to destroy it making art… something I used to do in a NY minute. 

I’m going to scan this magazine instead so I preserve the original. The intention is to have the collages with the scanned images at a lower price point than the canvases that have the original magazines as content. 

I slowed down doing mixed media collage because so many artists started creating collage. Especially within the African American art community. Note, I’ve been doing mixed media collage since I was in High school and this medium is nothing new to me. In collage my professor #TedBonavito showed me a few techniques and he is the one who inspired me to do collages. It was during this time I was studying and recognizing artist like #jacoblawrence #robertrauschenberg . @beardenfoundation_official bearden , @pablo___picasso and even @basquiatofficial. At the same time I was heavily influenced by pop culture and underground @graffiti. In my 30’s my gravitation to mixed was also to step away from my being compared local artists who also were influenced by pop culture, especially DJ Culture. I will expand on that at a later date. 

With all that said, 2025 is going to be interesting to say the least. As I see artists completely ripping or as they say in the streets, “biting” popular styles and trending artists, how am I going to make a mark in this over saturated art market place? The possibilities are endless & social media will play a big part in this on going experiment.

So let’s see what happens as I use social media to record the progress of this creative journey. 2024 I purposely focused on DJ Culture. 2025 I bring it all together!

